            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I realize this is WIP, but please ensure that the backend for this is actually usable and correct before moving this out of WIP."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Asmitha Karunanithi",
                        "email": "asmitk01@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "asmithakarun"
                    },
                    "message": "I have verified this with an OpenBMC image built for system1 and once with p10bmc to cover the use case where the interfaces are not present."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/71057 \nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/60582\n\nAre some previous commits in this area. \n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/62737 added slot information to pcie device \n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/62073/ and the one above were going to add empty pcie slots to the device collection"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/pcie_slots.hpp",
                    "line": 207,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please don't chain lambdas like this.  the old code was already correct, so please don't make it worse"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/pcie_slots.hpp",
                    "line": 207,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Asmitha Karunanithi",
                        "email": "asmitk01@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "asmithakarun"
                    },
                    "message": "Got it.\n\nBut, earlier all properties of only one interface was fetched and populated into Slots array. Now, for the same object, the other two interfaces' properties also should be fetched and populated into the same slot entry of the array.\n\nWill shorten the \"processPcieSlot\" method by having separate methods for each interface. Otherwise, do you think this still can be simplified?"
                }
            ],
